'''Treasure''' (お宝, ''Otakara'') is an important [[Stage Rewards|Stage Reward]] which may be obtained upon clearing stages in [[Empire of Cats]], [[Into the Future]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]]. Each stage in these areas has a Treasure named after a memento from the location, represented by a colored medal with a star. Each Treasure exists in up to 3 tiers, which are called '''Inferior''', '''Normal''', and '''Superior'''—their icons are colored bronze, silver and gold, respectively. Treasures are crucial for progression, so collecting them is a high priority whenever stages feel overwhelming.

Completing a regional collection of Treasures gives the player permanent upgrades to many aspects of the game, some of which do not have a counterpart in the XP-purchasable upgrades. Examples include massively increased [[Legendary Cat Shield|cat health]] or [[Legendary Cat Sword|attack power]], [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures|debuffs]] [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures|to]] [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]], or [[Fruit Treasures|improvements to certain abilities]]. The effect of the boost depends on the quality of the various Treasures in that collection. Obtaining all Superior Treasures in a chapter awards a massive amount of XP via [[Catnip Challenges]], peaking at 5,000,000 for [[Cats of the Cosmos]] Chapter 3.

Most activated Treasure effects are permanent for each player and carried through '''all stages''', including [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]], [[Legend Stages]], [[Catclaw Dojo]] and [[Underground Labyrinth]]; the effect then stacks additively with any other Treasure set effects already active or subsequently acquired. The only exception is the [[Mystery Mask]], which affects one chapter's final boss but not the others.

The [[Cat Units|Cat Unit]] and [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien enemy]] stats listed on this wiki are with all Treasures obtained, except when stated otherwise ("initial stats" are what a unit has at level 1 without any Treasures). ''Abilities'', however, are always described without the [[Fruit Treasures]]' bonuses.

==Obtaining Treasure==
Obtaining Treasure is paramount and a key aspect of [[The Battle Cats]] that must not be neglected if a player is to make any significant progress in the game. Without them, your units' stats such as health and attack will eventually prove insufficient, while Alien enemies and the Cats of the Cosmos final bosses have overwhelmingly powerful stats.

Treasure is awarded randomly after clearing each of the main story stages, and a small pop-up in the victory screen will indicate whether a Treasure has been obtained. It is possible for any tier of Treasure to drop; however, if a player has already obtained a Treasure from a particular stage, the game will not award Treasure of lower or equal tier. Players will often have to repeatedly clear a stage until they obtain the ''Superior'' Treasure.

By default, most stages have a 35% chance (70% during a [[Treasure Festival]]) to drop a Treasure, which then has a 45% chance to be Inferior, 30% for Normal, and 25% for Superior. If the stage's Inferior Treasure has already been obtained, the odds will change to a 70% chance of being Normal and 30% of being Superior.

