The only stage to have a different Treasure drop rate than usual is the first stage of [[Empire of Cats]], [[Korea (Empire of Cats)|Korea/Nagasaki]], which always guarantees a Superior Treasure in Chapter 1. Using a [[Battle Items#Treasure Radar|Treasure Radar]] will also guarantee a Superior Treasure upon victory, albeit at the cost of the Radar.

The Z-medals awarded from [[Zombie Outbreaks]] are different, given only as a Zombie Outbreak clearance stage reward. Thus, the player may obtain a stage Treasure and Zombie Outbreak clearance medal at the same time. Having all Zombie Outbreak Medals of a certain Treasure set will increase the Treasure drop rate of all stages involved by an unknown amount.

==Checking Treasures Obtained==
Once the player has obtained a Treasure from a stage, an icon corresponding to the Treasure tier will appear beside the stage name. The name of the Treasure can also be found in the collections screen.[[File:Treasure stage select.jpeg|thumb|centre|450px|class=large-image]]
<p style="text-align: center;">''The stage selection screen shows stages from which Treasures have already been obtained—note the gold Treasure icons beside the stage names which mean that the player has obtained the Superior Treasures.''</p>

Players can check the Treasures they have already obtained along with the activated Treasure effects if the set is complete, by selecting the Menu icon on the Chapter dashboard then selecting the Treasure option.

