==Treasure Festivals==
''Refer to the [[Treasure Festival]] page''

Every once in a while, a Treasure Festival will appear, which "doubles" (read: increases) the chances of you acquiring a treasure from a stage. When there is a specific chance for Treasure from a certain location (e.g., [[Korea (Empire of Cats)|Korea/Nagasaki]]) then pressing the icon will take you directly to that location.

These all-stage festivals generally last for an hour and appear randomly throughout the day, but sometimes there is a Monthly Event or SNS promotion that grants a festival for Empire of Cats on odd days of the month and Into the Future on even days of the month (or vice-versa) and will really benefit you if you can line up the timeline with your schedule. Every month on the 22nd is [[Meow Meow Day]], which has a 24-hour Treasure Festival for all of the main story chapters.

===Individual Stage Treasure Festivals===
There are also Treasure Festivals that pop up for specific stages, that are chosen randomly and generally only last for 30 minutes. These are not a part of the event Calendar.

Be aware that the Treasure Festival icon on your map may be hiding a [[Zombie Outbreaks|Zombie Outbreak]] stage, so check thoroughly when it's festival time—you may get a medal and Treasure all at once! You may log in to [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 3 to find that you have a treasure festival on [[Saudi Arabia (Empire of Cats)|Saudi Arabia/Shimane]] and completely miss out on the Outbreak stage back at [[China (Empire of Cats)|China/Kagoshima]].

== Treasure Gauge ==
Introduced [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], The Treasure Gauge is a small bar that appears at the top of the stage selection screen. You can fill it up by doing certain actions in the game. Once it reaches 100 points, the next stage you clear in [[Empire of Cats]], [[Into the Future]], or [[Cats of the Cosmos]] will give you a guaranteed superior treasure. You can also tap the Treasure Gauge icon to open the Treasure Menu and check which treasures you’re still missing.

