==Treasure Mechanics==
The bonus applied from any set of Treasures is only activated upon obtaining all the separate parts of the set. The total activated effect (or power) is then shown as a percentage of the maximum effect possible from that set.

Each Treasure contributes to the set's effectiveness percentage based on its tier.
*Bronze-tier Inferior Treasures award an inferior boost.
*Silver-tier Normal Treasures award a moderate boost.
*Gold-tier Superior Treasures award a superior boost.
To obtain the full 100% power of the Treasure set, the player needs to obtain all the Superior Treasures in the collection.

It's important to understand that when the Treasure set's power percentage reaches 100%, this does not imply that the effect of the Treasure set will increase the relevant stat by 100%. It simply refers to the Treasure set being applied with maximum effect or with 100% power.

The formula for the percentage activation:

<math>
\text{Activation }\% = \dfrac{\text{Sum of Treasure tier values}}{3\cdot\text{Number of Treasures in set}}
</math>
*Treasure values: Inferior=1, Normal=2, Superior=3

Example:

Empire of Cats' [[Energy Drink]] requires 7 Treasures to be obtained before its effect is activated.
[[File:Energy Drink Activated.png|thumb|left|390px|class=large-image]]
